{"kind":"finding","id":"FN-B-switch-phone-tracker-components-1-b-01","date":"2026-11-26","lens":"gap-6","surface":"phone","area":"phone/tracker-components-1","refs":["F-phone-713","F-phone-732","F-phone-733","F-phone-701","FN-B-switch-phone-screens-1-b-01"],"severity":"S4","title":"Workout time, length, machine and weigh-in fix boxes drop or refuse numbers in Hindi digits","what":"The start time, minutes and length boxes on Log a past workout and on Correct a saved workout keep only the digits 0-9, and so do the speed, incline and level boxes on a cardio set. A number typed on a keyboard set to Hindi digits, or pasted from a Hindi message, is dropped as it is typed, so the box stays empty. The Fix this weigh-in box keeps what was typed but then refuses it with 'Type a number above 0'. The mobile number boxes in the same app already turn Hindi digits into 0-9.","expected":"Hindi and other Indian-script digits are turned into 0-9 before these boxes clean or read the number.","evidence":["apps/mobile/src/tracker/components/LogPastSheet.tsx:151-175","apps/mobile/src/tracker/components/EditSessionHeader.tsx:154-185","apps/mobile/src/tracker/services/editFields.ts:49-54","apps/mobile/src/tracker/components/MachineDetailsRow.tsx:96-103","apps/mobile/src/tracker/engine/cardioMachine.ts:99-105","apps/mobile/src/tracker/components/BodyEntrySheet.tsx:74-82","apps/mobile/src/app/measures/index.tsx:142-145","packages/theme/src/indianMobile.ts:108-111"],"proof":"code-read","root_cause_key":"time-boxes-drop-indian-digits","who":"members who type or paste Hindi digits","how_often":"every time such a number is entered","fix_line":"Convert Indian-script digits to 0-9 first in these boxes, using the same step the mobile boxes use","fix_size":"small","needs_him":false,"verified":"pending","status":"open"}
